<http://data.silknow.org/object/b62200e1-7300-37a1-8f46-d23b7dab4203>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Cream fingerless mittens made of machine knitted silk."@en , "Pair of fingerless mittens, cream machine knitted silk, made in England, 1840-1850"@en , "Mittens were a popular lightweight alternative to gloves for  women, freeing their fingers for embroidery and other  domestic tasks.\nMittens were made from soft leather, silk or knitted silk and were usually elbow-length. In the mid-19th century mittens were worn mainly by older women, while younger ones had adopted the French taste for embroidered kid gloves."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/b6d40e79-3f26-3781-a5ca-40f8a16db187> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/66fd4faa-bba5-3308-aa10-934af3d87d62> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Mittens were a popular lightweight alternative to gloves for  women, freeing their fingers for embroidery and other  domestic tasks.\nMittens were made from soft leather, silk or knitted silk and were usually elbow-length. In the mid-19th century mittens were worn mainly by older women, while younger ones had adopted the French taste for embroidered kid gloves."@en , "Pair of fingerless mittens, cream machine knitted silk, made in England, 1840-1850"@en , "Cream fingerless mittens made of machine knitted silk."@en ;
